Kill the bastard.

489
00:44:07,474 --> 00:44:08,964
Nobody knows who he is.

490
00:44:10,724 --> 00:44:12,931
Have you brought
any fruits or vegetables?

491
00:44:13,141 --> 00:44:14,927
Two weeks.

492
00:44:16,224 --> 00:44:17,555
Excuse me?

493
00:44:17,766 --> 00:44:20,223
Two weeks.

494
00:44:21,391 --> 00:44:23,552
Two weeks!

495
00:44:27,391 --> 00:44:32,055
It's not just graffiti. The rebels
took over the refinery last night.

496
00:44:32,266 --> 00:44:34,131
No terbinium is going out.

497
00:44:34,349 --> 00:44:35,805
And it gets worse.

498
00:44:36,016 --> 00:44:37,927
T-w-0...

499
00:44:56,391 --> 00:44:57,597
Quaid.

500
00:44:58,891 --> 00:45:00,427
- That's quaid!
- Where?

501
00:45:00,641 --> 00:45:02,177
The woman! Get him... her!

502
00:45:03,349 --> 00:45:04,759
Arrest that woman!

503
00:45:04,974 --> 00:45:06,305
Get that woman. Grab her!

504
00:45:36,224 --> 00:45:37,224
Catch!

505
00:45:39,558 --> 00:45:41,594
Get ready for a surprise!

506
00:46:27,308 --> 00:46:28,308
Ah!

507
00:46:52,391 --> 00:46:54,382
- Open the goddamn door!
- I can't!

508
00:46:54,599 --> 00:46:55,759
Open it!

509
00:46:55,974 --> 00:46:57,760
They're all connected!

510
00:47:07,058 --> 00:47:08,343
That's terrible.

511
00:47:08,558 --> 00:47:10,438
A few days ago
cohaagen raised the price of air.

512
00:47:10,641 --> 00:47:11,756
Again?

513
00:47:11,974 --> 00:47:14,215
Nobody on earth gives a damn
what happens up here.

514
00:47:14,433 --> 00:47:16,845
They just want our terbinium
so they can fight their war.

515
00:47:17,058 --> 00:47:18,923
Excuse me. What's that?

516
00:47:19,141 --> 00:47:21,132
You mean the pyramid mine?

517
00:47:21,349 --> 00:47:24,671
I used to work there until
they found that alien shit inside.

518
00:47:24,891 --> 00:47:27,132
Well, that's a rumor, isn't it?

519
00:47:27,474 --> 00:47:28,589
Think so?

520
00:47:58,349 --> 00:47:59,634
Mr cohaagen.

521
00:48:07,266 --> 00:48:09,382
You wanted to see me, sir?

522
00:48:12,766 --> 00:48:14,176
Richter...

523
00:48:15,474 --> 00:48:17,339
Do you know why
I'm such a happy person?

524
00:48:17,558 --> 00:48:18,843
No, sir.

525
00:48:21,058 --> 00:48:24,255
Because I've got the greatest job
in the solar system.

526
00:48:24,474 --> 00:48:28,262
As long as the terbinium keeps flowing,
I can do anything I want.

527
00:48:28,683 --> 00:48:30,264
Anything.

528
00:48:31,641 --> 00:48:34,713
In fact, the only thing
that I ever worry about

529
00:48:34,933 --> 00:48:40,257
is that one day, if the rebels win,
it all might end...

530
00:48:41,474 --> 00:48:42,930
And you're fucking making it happen!

531
00:48:44,183 --> 00:48:47,016
First you try to kill quaid,
then you let him get away.

532
00:48:47,224 --> 00:48:49,465
He had help from our side, sir.

533
00:48:50,558 --> 00:48:51,593
I know that.

534
00:48:54,058 --> 00:48:56,014
- But I thought...
- Who told you to think?

535
00:48:56,224 --> 00:48:59,182
I don't give you enough information
to think.

536
00:49:01,391 --> 00:49:04,383
You do what you're told.
That's what you do.

537
00:49:06,933 --> 00:49:08,343
Yes, sir.

538
00:49:09,058 --> 00:49:10,969
Now...

539
00:49:13,266 --> 00:49:14,756
Let's get to business.

540
00:49:16,641 --> 00:49:18,848
We've got a tricky situation here.

541
00:49:19,058 --> 00:49:21,265
Kuato wants what's in quaid's head.

542
00:49:23,058 --> 00:49:25,925
And he might be able to get it,
cos they say he's psychic.

543
00:49:27,641 --> 00:49:30,678
And I have a plan
to keep this from happening.

544
00:49:34,183 --> 00:49:35,639
Do you think you could play along?

545
00:49:35,849 --> 00:49:37,840
- Yes, sir.
- Great.

546
00:49:38,058 --> 00:49:40,390
Cos otherwise, I'll erase your ass.

547
00:49:55,308 --> 00:49:58,630
You've got some
identification? Yeah, you too.

548
00:49:58,849 --> 00:50:02,717
Taxi? You need a taxi, sir?
I got magazines, music, whisky.

549
00:50:02,933 --> 00:50:05,470
Hey, man, you need a cab, man?
Come on! Come on!

550
00:50:30,516 --> 00:50:32,131
Good afternoon. Can I help you?

551
00:50:32,349 --> 00:50:34,761
Yes, I would like
to have a room, please.

552
00:50:40,349 --> 00:50:42,949
Nice to have you back, mr brubaker.
Would you like the same suite?

553
00:50:43,016 --> 00:50:44,722
Oh, definitely.

554
00:50:46,724 --> 00:50:48,806
Seems you've left something
in our safe.

555
00:50:49,016 --> 00:50:51,007
Could you get it, please?

556
00:50:56,058 --> 00:50:57,514
Identification?

557
00:51:07,141 --> 00:51:09,974
- I'll encode your room key.
- Thank you.

558
00:51:25,849 --> 00:51:29,262
- Suite 610 in the east wing.
- Thank you.

559
00:51:29,474 --> 00:51:32,056
- Could I borrow your pen, please?
- Certainly.

560
00:51:43,808 --> 00:51:44,843
Thank you.

561
00:51:50,308 --> 00:51:52,640
Hey, man, you need a cab?

562
00:51:52,849 --> 00:51:57,172
- What's wrong with this one?
- He ain't got five kids to feed.

563
00:51:57,391 --> 00:52:00,463
- Where's yours?
- Right over there, man.

564
00:52:00,683 --> 00:52:02,719
Hey! Hey, man.

565
00:52:02,933 --> 00:52:04,673
Hey, asshole! That's my fare!

566
00:52:04,891 --> 00:52:07,303
- Eat this!
- Damn you, Benny!

567
00:52:13,933 --> 00:52:15,298
Welcome to Mars, man!

568
00:52:19,641 --> 00:52:21,131
What the hell was that, an accident?

569
00:52:21,349 --> 00:52:24,637
That's the rebels, man.
Let's get outta here...

570
00:52:24,849 --> 00:52:26,589
Before they arrest us!

571
00:52:26,808 --> 00:52:28,469
What do the rebels want?

572
00:52:28,683 --> 00:52:32,005
The usual.
More money, more freedom, more air.

573
00:52:37,224 --> 00:52:38,339
So, where to?

574
00:52:38,558 --> 00:52:40,173
Last resort.

575
00:52:40,391 --> 00:52:42,256
You're getting off to an early start.

576
00:52:43,391 --> 00:52:45,552
- First time on Mars?
- Yes.

577
00:52:45,766 --> 00:52:48,963
Well, actually, no. Well, sort of.

578
00:52:49,183 --> 00:52:53,256
The man don't even know
whether he's been to Mars or not.

579
00:53:03,891 --> 00:53:06,223
Voila. Venusyville.

580
00:53:06,433 --> 00:53:09,630
Ha, ha!
Hey, you see anything you like?

581
00:53:13,974 --> 00:53:17,011
Well, this is the end of the line.
We'd better walk from here.

582
00:53:17,224 --> 00:53:19,089
I'll show you where.

583
00:53:19,308 --> 00:53:22,800
- Do you want to know the future?
- What about the past?

584
00:53:23,016 --> 00:53:26,634
Come on. It's around the corner,
right down this alley.

585
00:53:26,849 --> 00:53:28,885
They got everything.

586
00:53:31,558 --> 00:53:33,139
Not bad, huh?

587
00:53:34,891 --> 00:53:39,214
Read your palm? Your mind? Your aura?
Probe the secrets of your heart?

588
00:53:39,433 --> 00:53:41,515
I bet I can guess your birthday.

589
00:53:41,724 --> 00:53:44,841
- You're a Taurus, right?
- How did you guess?

590
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:49,510
- Tell me, are all psychics...?
- Freaks?

591
00:53:49,724 --> 00:53:51,635
Afraid so, man.
It goes with the territory.

592
00:53:51,849 --> 00:53:56,718
- What happened to them?
- Cheap domes, no air to clean the rays.

593
00:53:56,933 --> 00:54:00,755
So, this is it. The last resort.
You sure you want to go in here?

594
00:54:00,974 --> 00:54:04,296
- Why not?
- There's a better place down there.

595
00:54:04,516 --> 00:54:07,132
The girls are cleaner,
the liquor ain't watered down...

596
00:54:07,349 --> 00:54:09,635
Sure, and you get kickbacks.

597
00:54:09,849 --> 00:54:12,636
Hey, man, I got five kids to feed.

598
00:54:12,849 --> 00:54:14,305
Take them to the dentist.

599
00:54:14,516 --> 00:54:17,007
Hey, thanks, mister!
I'll be waiting for you.

600
00:54:17,224 --> 00:54:19,306
You just take your time.
Benny's the name.

601
00:54:39,599 --> 00:54:41,510
- What do you want?
- I'm looking for Melina.

602
00:54:41,724 --> 00:54:43,385
She's busy.

603
00:54:43,599 --> 00:54:45,260
But Mary here, she's free.

604
00:54:46,183 --> 00:54:48,765
Well, not free, honey, but...

605
00:54:49,683 --> 00:54:51,093
Available.

606
00:54:51,933 --> 00:54:53,764
Ha-ha-ha!

607
00:54:53,974 --> 00:54:56,215
Thanks. I'll wait for Melina.

608
00:54:56,433 --> 00:54:57,513
Earth slime.

609
00:54:57,724 --> 00:55:00,261
Thing is, friend, Mel's real picky.

610
00:55:00,474 --> 00:55:02,681
She kind of sticks to her regulars.

611
00:55:02,891 --> 00:55:04,347
She'll like me.

612
00:55:05,891 --> 00:55:07,051
Mel!

613
00:55:07,266 --> 00:55:08,756
Hey, Mel!

614
00:55:44,808 --> 00:55:46,389
Hello, hauser.

615
00:55:47,391 --> 00:55:49,006
Still bulging, I see.

616
00:55:50,599 --> 00:55:53,716
- What you been feeding this thing?
- Blondes.

617
00:55:55,683 --> 00:55:57,844
I think it's still hungry.

618
00:56:00,183 --> 00:56:03,016
You got a lot of nerve
showing your face around here, hauser.

619
00:56:03,224 --> 00:56:05,089
Look who's talking.

620
00:56:05,308 --> 00:56:08,015
Hey, Tony,
give the big guy a break.

621
00:56:08,224 --> 00:56:10,431
Relax. You'll live longer.

622
00:56:10,641 --> 00:56:12,381
Come on.

623
00:56:17,683 --> 00:56:20,846
- Honey, take care of Tony, will you?
- No problem.

624
00:56:21,349 --> 00:56:24,466
If you need any help with this one,
give me a holler.

625
00:56:39,349 --> 00:56:41,135
You son of a bitch.

626
00:56:41,349 --> 00:56:43,931
You're alive? I thought that
cohaagen tortured you to death.

627
00:56:44,141 --> 00:56:45,881
Well, I guess he didn't.

628
00:56:46,099 --> 00:56:49,796
And you couldn't get me a message?
You never wondered what happened to me?

629
00:56:57,474 --> 00:56:59,681
Hauser, thank god you're alive.

630
00:57:00,891 --> 00:57:03,132
Melin... Melina. Melina.

631
00:57:04,141 --> 00:57:08,009
- Melina, I have to tell you something.
- What?

632
00:57:08,224 --> 00:57:11,671
- I don't remember you.
- What are you talking about?

633
00:57:11,891 --> 00:57:13,973
I don't remember you.

634
00:57:14,183 --> 00:57:17,425
I don't remember us.
I don't even remember me.

635
00:57:19,683 --> 00:57:21,924
Did you get amnesia?
How did you get here?

636
00:57:22,141 --> 00:57:24,382
- Hauser left me a note.
- Hauser? You're hauser.

637
00:57:24,599 --> 00:57:26,430
Not anymore.

638
00:57:26,641 --> 00:57:29,599
Now I'm quaid. Douglas quaid.

639
00:57:32,891 --> 00:57:36,839
- Hauser, you've lost your mind.
- I didn't. Cohaagen stole it.

640
00:57:37,058 --> 00:57:41,472
He found out that hauser switched sides,
so he turned him into somebody else: Me.

641
00:57:41,683 --> 00:57:43,014
This is too weird.

642
00:57:43,224 --> 00:57:45,590
He dumped me on earth
with a wife and a lousy job...

643
00:57:45,808 --> 00:57:48,595
Did you say wife?
Are you fucking married?

644
00:57:48,808 --> 00:57:50,719
- She wasn't really my wife.
- Oh, she isn't?

645
00:57:50,933 --> 00:57:53,140
How stupid of me.
She was hauser's wife?

646
00:57:53,349 --> 00:57:56,307
- Look. Forget that I said wife.
- Let's just forget everything.

647
00:57:56,516 --> 00:58:00,054
- I'm sick of hearing your goddamn lies.
- Why would I lie to you?

648
00:58:01,183 --> 00:58:04,425
Because you're still
working for cohaagen.

649
00:58:04,641 --> 00:58:06,552
Don't be ridiculous.

650
00:58:09,933 --> 00:58:11,924
You never loved me, hauser.

651
00:58:12,141 --> 00:58:14,006
You just used me to get inside.

652
00:58:14,224 --> 00:58:16,180
Inside what?

653
00:58:20,266 --> 00:58:22,222
I think you'd better leave.

654
00:58:22,433 --> 00:58:25,470
- Hauser sent me to do something.
- I'm not falling for it.

655
00:58:25,683 --> 00:58:27,923
He says there's enough in here
to nail cohaagen for good.

656
00:58:28,016 --> 00:58:29,802
- Get out!
- You've got to help me remember!

657
00:58:30,016 --> 00:58:32,098
- I said, get out!
- Melina, please!

658
00:58:32,308 --> 00:58:33,969
People are trying to kill me.

659
00:58:34,974 --> 00:58:36,054
Really?

660
00:58:38,974 --> 00:58:40,930
All right, I'm leaving.

661
00:58:52,808 --> 00:58:55,845
Baby, you make me wish
I had three hands.

662
00:58:56,058 --> 00:58:58,640
I think you're doing
just fine with two.

663
00:58:58,849 --> 00:59:01,090
Excuse me, baby.
We'll pick this up later.

664
00:59:01,308 --> 00:59:03,594
Hey, that didn't take long.

665
00:59:03,808 --> 00:59:06,265
Listen. Let me ask you a question.
Did you ever fuck a mutant?

666
00:59:06,474 --> 00:59:08,806
- Take me to the hotel.
- I know these siamese twins.

667
00:59:09,016 --> 00:59:12,053
Man, you won't know
if you're coming or going.

668
00:59:21,391 --> 00:59:25,009
'This afternoon at 4:30pm,
I signed an order declaring martial law

669
00:59:25,224 --> 00:59:27,260
'throughout the Mars federal colony.

670
00:59:27,474 --> 00:59:32,173
'I will not tolerate any further damage
to our mineral export operations.

671
00:59:32,391 --> 00:59:34,347
'Mr kuato and his terrorists
must understand

672
00:59:34,558 --> 00:59:38,176
'that their self-defeating efforts
will only bring misery and suffering..."

673
00:59:41,808 --> 00:59:44,595
- Mr quaid?
- What?

674
00:59:44,808 --> 00:59:47,595
I need to talk to you
about mr hauser.

675
00:59:48,516 --> 00:59:50,677
- Who are you?
- Dr edgemar from recall.

676
00:59:50,891 --> 00:59:53,007
- How did you find me?
- It's difficult to explain.

677
00:59:53,224 --> 00:59:56,296
Could you open the door?
I'm unarmed.

678
00:59:58,349 --> 01:00:00,681
Don't worry. I'm alone.
May I come in?

679
01:00:02,599 --> 01:00:03,759
What do you want?

680
01:00:03,974 --> 01:00:06,367
This is going to be very difficult
for you to accept, mr quaid.

681
01:00:06,391 --> 01:00:11,306
- I'm listening.
- You're not really standing here now.

682
01:00:11,516 --> 01:00:14,474
- Doc, you could have fooled me.
- I'm quite serious.

683
01:00:14,683 --> 01:00:17,720
You're not here and neither am I.

684
01:00:17,933 --> 01:00:19,218
That's amazing.

685
01:00:19,433 --> 01:00:22,049
- Where are we?
- At recall.

686
01:00:22,683 --> 01:00:24,219
You're strapped into
an implant chair,

687
01:00:24,433 --> 01:00:27,675
and I'm monitoring you
from the psychoprobe console.

688
01:00:28,683 --> 01:00:31,049
Ah, I get it. I'm dreaming.

689
01:00:31,266 --> 01:00:34,429
And all this is part of the delightful
vacation your company has sold me.

690
01:00:34,641 --> 01:00:35,926
Not exactly.

691
01:00:36,141 --> 01:00:40,180
What you're experiencing is a free-form
delusion based on our memory tapes

692
01:00:40,391 --> 01:00:43,349
but you're inventing it yourself
as you go along.

693
01:00:44,474 --> 01:00:47,796
If it is my delusion,
who the hell invited you?

694
01:00:48,016 --> 01:00:51,634
I've been artificially implanted
as an emergency measure.

695
01:00:51,849 --> 01:00:55,091
I'm sorry to tell you this,
but you've suffered a schizoid embolism.

696
01:00:55,308 --> 01:00:57,469
We can't snap you
out of your fantasy,

697
01:00:57,683 --> 01:01:00,755
and I've been sent in
to try to talk you down.

698
01:01:00,974 --> 01:01:02,635
How much is cohaagen
paying you for this?

699
01:01:04,224 --> 01:01:08,297
Think about it. Your dream started
in the middle of the implant procedure.

700
01:01:08,516 --> 01:01:10,723
Everything after that,
the chases, the trip to Mars,

701
01:01:10,933 --> 01:01:15,302
the suite at the Hilton, are elements
of your recall holiday and ego trip.

702
01:01:15,516 --> 01:01:17,757
You paid to be a secret agent.

703
01:01:17,974 --> 01:01:20,340
Bullshit. It's coincidence.

704
01:01:21,183 --> 01:01:23,174
And what about the girl?

705
01:01:23,391 --> 01:01:25,882
Brunette, athletic,
sleazy and demure?

706
01:01:26,099 --> 01:01:28,431
Just as you specified.
Is that coincidence?

707
01:01:28,641 --> 01:01:32,133
She's real. I dreamt about her
before I even went to recall.

708
01:01:32,349 --> 01:01:34,305
Ha, mr quaid.

709
01:01:34,516 --> 01:01:38,429
Can you hear yourself?
She's real because you dreamed her?

710
01:01:38,641 --> 01:01:41,508
- That's right.
- Maybe this will convince you.

711
01:01:42,391 --> 01:01:44,598
Would you mind opening the door?

712
01:01:46,099 --> 01:01:50,547
- You open it.
- No need to be rude. I'll do it.

713
01:01:56,974 --> 01:01:58,134
Sweetheart?

714
01:02:00,808 --> 01:02:03,174
Come in, mrs quaid.

715
01:02:07,058 --> 01:02:11,677
- I suppose you're not here either.
- I'm here... at recall.

716
01:02:16,391 --> 01:02:18,052
I love you.

717
01:02:18,266 --> 01:02:21,463
Right.
That's why you tried to kill me.

718
01:02:21,683 --> 01:02:24,720
No. I'd never do anything
to hurt you.

719
01:02:25,724 --> 01:02:28,181
I want you to come back to me.

720
01:02:30,266 --> 01:02:33,383
- Bullshit.
- What's bullshit, mr quaid?

721
01:02:33,599 --> 01:02:35,385
That you're having
a paranoid episode

722
01:02:35,599 --> 01:02:38,136
triggered by acute
neurochemical trauma?

723
01:02:38,349 --> 01:02:42,171
Or that you're really an invincible
secret agent from Mars,

724
01:02:42,391 --> 01:02:46,384
who's the victim of an interplanetary
conspiracy to make him think

725
01:02:46,599 --> 01:02:48,430
he's a lowly construction worker?

726
01:02:56,099 --> 01:02:58,306
Stop punishing yourself, Doug.

727
01:02:58,516 --> 01:03:01,349
You're a fine, upstanding man.
You have a beautiful wife who loves you.

728
01:03:02,974 --> 01:03:04,839
- Your whole life is ahead of you.
- I do.

729
01:03:06,933 --> 01:03:09,470
But you've got to want
to return to reality.

730
01:03:11,891 --> 01:03:14,473
Let's assume I do. Then what?

731
01:03:17,391 --> 01:03:20,383
- Swallow this.
- What is it?

732
01:03:20,599 --> 01:03:23,796
It's a symbol of your desire
to return to reality.

733
